  "id": "Tropical_Blend_Cyber_Politics_Ramp_Up_Across_Latin_America_txt_9",
  "content": "Geopolitics has focused major nation-states on the Latin America and Caribbean region. The US military operation to capture the president of Venezuela and his wife and the Trump administration's vow to \"take back\" the Panama Canal are among the US-China points of tension that may spur additional cyber activity, experts say. China holds claims to about half the oil produced by Venezuela, and the Chinese company that held the contracts to operate ports on both sides of the Panama Canal — the Panama Ports Company, a subsidiary of the Hong Kong-based conglomerate CK Hutchison — lost its contract when the country's Supreme Court ruled that the agreement violated Panama's constitution .",
